-- title:
--   Flat condition of type S detected on Artinian quotients
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring with an algebra structure on $A$, let $p$ be a natural number and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers, and let $\rho$ be an object of [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16): a free finite $A$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_A V = 2$, together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\operatorname{End}_A V$ that is adically continuous, i.e. for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak m_A^n V$ for all $v$. Assume that for every $m$ the reduction of $\rho$ along the (local, surjective) projection $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A^{m+1}$, obtained by tensoring $V$ and base-changing each $\rho(\sigma)$, satisfies [`GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47), that is: its determinant is cyclotomic at $p$ (the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal, and $\det \rho(\sigma) - a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$ whenever $\sigma$ raises all $p^n$-th roots of unity to the $a$-th power), it is flat at $p$ (the residue field is finite and, for every ideal $I$ with finite quotient, there is a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra $H$ over [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points, taken in `WithConv`, correspond additively and Galois-equivariantly to $V/IV$), and it is unramified at every prime $q \notin S$ (inertia at every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $q$ acts trivially). Then $\rho$ itself satisfies [`GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47).
--
--   This is the continuity clause for the flat deformation condition of type $S$ at $p$ in the sense of Mazur's deformation conditions: the condition on a representation over a Noetherian local ring is detected on its reductions modulo the powers of the maximal ideal. It is used to supply that clause in [`GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_flatCondition`](thm.html#GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_flatCondition).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_flatCondition_of_forall_quotient.lean

import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_Flat

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem GaloisRepAdic.flatCondition_of_forall_quotient
    {A : Type} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (𝒪 : Type) [CommRing 𝒪] [Algebra 𝒪 A] (ρ : GaloisRepAdic A) {p : ℕ} {S : Finset ℕ}
    (h : ∀ m : ℕ,
      haveI : Nontrivial (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)) :=
        Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr (ne_top_of_le_ne_top
          (Ideal.IsMaximal.ne_top inferInstance) (Ideal.pow_le_self (Nat.succ_ne_zero m)))
      haveI : IsLocalRing (A ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)) :=
        IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
      GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪 p S
        (ρ.baseChangeAlong (Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ (m + 1)))
          (IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective))) :
    GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪 p S ρ := by sorry
